---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Shot from "../components/Shot.astro";
import { GUIDE, ARCHITECTURE } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title="How it works"
  description="A daemon owns the sessions, each agent runs in a pane of rlord's own tmux server, and the overlord is one agent session with rlord's tools."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h1>A daemon, tmux and one overlord</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A daemon owns the sessions. Each agent runs in a pane of rlord's own tmux server. The overlord is one agent
        session with rlord's tools.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <figure class="diagram" style="margin:0">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 760 440" role="img" aria-labelledby="diagram-title diagram-desc">
          <title id="diagram-title">How rlord's parts connect</title>
          <desc id="diagram-desc">
            You use the list or, with Option-O, the overlord. The overlord delegates to subagents and reaches the
            rlord daemon through MCP tools. The daemon runs claude, codex and opencode in its own tmux server.
          </desc>
          <defs>
            <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto">
              <path class="arrowhead" d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z"></path>
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <rect class="box" x="225" y="6" width="110" height="36" rx="18"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="280" y="29">You</text>
          <path class="line" d="M280 42V58H140V82" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <path class="line" d="M280 58H420V82" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <text class="s" x="472" y="68">Option-O</text>

          <rect class="box" x="50" y="84" width="180" height="64" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="140" y="112">The list</text>
          <text class="s" x="140" y="132">terminal UI</text>

          <rect class="box red" x="320" y="84" width="200" height="64" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t on-dark" x="420" y="112">Overlord</text>
          <text class="s on-dark" x="420" y="132">medium effort</text>

          <path class="line" d="M520 116H588" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <text class="s" x="554" y="106">delegates</text>
          <rect class="box" x="590" y="84" width="160" height="64" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="670" y="112">Subagents</text>
          <text class="s" x="670" y="132">tidy, import, research</text>

          <path class="line" d="M140 148V208" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <path class="line" d="M420 148V208" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <text class="s" x="466" y="184">MCP tools</text>

          <rect class="box inverse" x="50" y="210" width="700" height="64" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t on-inverse" x="400" y="238">rlord daemon</text>
          <text class="s on-inverse" x="400" y="258">sessions, status, search, summaries</text>

          <path class="line" d="M400 274V318"></path>
          <text class="s" x="476" y="302">its own tmux server</text>
          <path class="line" d="M130 356V318H670V356" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <path class="line" d="M130 318V356" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <path class="line" d="M310 318V356" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>
          <path class="line" d="M490 318V356" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></path>

          <rect class="box" x="60" y="358" width="140" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="130" y="386">claude</text>
          <rect class="box" x="240" y="358" width="140" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="310" y="386">codex</text>
          <rect class="box" x="420" y="358" width="140" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="490" y="386">opencode</text>
          <rect class="box" x="600" y="358" width="140" height="44" rx="8" stroke-dasharray="5 4"></rect>
          <text class="s" x="670" y="385">more sessions</text>
        </svg>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2 id="daemon">The daemon</h2>
      <p>
        A daemon owns everything. It keeps the session database and follows each agent's state through Claude Code's
        and Codex's hooks and OpenCode's own server. It serves the list, the CLI and the overlord over one local
        socket. It starts by itself the first time you run <code>rlord</code>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sessions">Sessions</h2>
      <p>
        Sessions are the ordinary agent CLIs. Each runs in a pane of rlord's own tmux server
        (<code>tmux -L rlord</code>). Your own tmux is never touched.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stopping and resuming uses the agent's own resume: <code>claude --resume</code>, <code>codex resume</code>
        and OpenCode's <code>-s</code>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="overlord">The overlord</h2>
      <p>
        The overlord is one agent session with rlord's tools, which are an MCP server. It opens over whatever you
        are looking at. You choose which agent runs it: Claude Code, Codex or OpenCode.
      </p>
      <p>
        It runs a strong model at medium effort. Look-ups, small edits and short answers it does itself. Anything
        that takes more goes to a subagent or a new session. That keeps it quick and keeps its own conversation
        small.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <Shot
        name="list"
        alt="The session list with the overlord's row selected. The details pane lists the overlord's earlier conversations."
        caption="The overlord's row in the list. The details pane lists its earlier conversations."
      />
    </div>

    <div class="wrap prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <h2 id="fresh">Fresh conversations</h2>
      <p>
        After 15 idle minutes rlord restarts the overlord on a fresh conversation, so its context does not grow
        without end. Nothing is carried over. When you refer to something from before, it looks it up in its own
        earlier conversations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The list shows when the current conversation started and how many came before. You can read an earlier
        conversation or continue it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="passing-work">Passing work to a session</h2>
      <p>
        The overlord can pass work to any session, whatever agent runs either. rlord types the message into that
        session's prompt once its turn is over.
      </p>
      <p>
        It does this without asking. rlord expects to be run by its user on a machine they trust, or over a remote
        connection they trust. Set <code>confirm_sends = true</code> under <code>[overlord]</code> to make each send
        ask first.
      </p>

      <h2 id="plain-code">Plain code first</h2>
      <p>
        The expensive part stays small. Questions like "which sessions changed since I last looked?" or "what did we
        say about this earlier?" are answered by plain code. The overlord spends tokens only on what needs judgment.
      </p>

      <h2 id="more">More detail</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href={GUIDE}>user guide</a> covers each part in detail. The{" "}
        <a href={ARCHITECTURE}>architecture document</a> explains the design.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
